1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,200
[The D Dorm]

2
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:04,800
♫Ho-hi, ho-hi, ho-hi, ho...♫

3
00:00:05,520 --> 00:00:07,960
- ♫Whoo!♫
- ♫Whoo!♫

4
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:10,560
- ♫Give us your lime♫
- ♫For a lemon♫

5
00:00:10,560 --> 00:00:11,720
♫Those who have a daughter♫

6
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:12,660
♫Let’s trade for a son-in-law♫

7
00:00:12,660 --> 00:00:14,660
♫Come now, this guard is your in-law♫

8
00:00:14,660 --> 00:00:16,580
- ♫Talala♫
- ♫Talala♫

9
00:00:16,580 --> 00:00:20,020
♫Ba dum pum, pum, pum♫

10
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:22,150
♫When will you accept my love?♫

11
00:00:22,150 --> 00:00:23,780
- Ugh!
- Whoa...

12
00:00:23,780 --> 00:00:24,720
What are you guys doing?

13
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:26,040
You guys are so loud.

14
00:00:26,040 --> 00:00:27,080
You too, Handyman Daeng.

15
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:28,770
Why don't you stop your brother?

16
00:00:28,890 --> 00:00:30,340
Why do I have to stop him?

17
00:00:30,550 --> 00:00:32,800
Since my brother is handsome...

18
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:34,010
cute,

19
00:00:34,010 --> 00:00:35,350
kind-hearted,

20
00:00:35,530 --> 00:00:37,750
and his heart is yours alone.

21
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:39,660
He has lots of love to give you.

22
00:00:39,660 --> 00:00:42,180
I think what he has are diseases.

23
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:43,600
From diabetes to

24
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:44,680
- blocked arteries
- Don't listen to her.

25
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:47,240
to high blood pressure!

26
00:00:47,240 --> 00:00:50,210
♫Ba dum pum, pum, pum...♫

27
00:00:50,210 --> 00:00:50,680
Hey!

28
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:52,920
You're acting like you're annoyed,

29
00:00:52,920 --> 00:00:54,120
but you played along, huh?

30
00:00:54,410 --> 00:00:54,760
Oops...

31
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:56,840
If you have that many diseases,
why don't you see a doctor?

32
00:00:56,840 --> 00:00:57,900
I did, but...

33
00:00:57,900 --> 00:00:58,530
But?

34
00:00:58,530 --> 00:01:03,380
- ♫Long time no see, I missed you so much♫
- ♫So much♫

35
00:01:03,380 --> 00:01:04,150
Hey!

36
00:01:04,450 --> 00:01:05,349
Stop playing along with them.

37
00:01:05,349 --> 00:01:06,220
I'm glad that you're here.

38
00:01:06,220 --> 00:01:07,360
I want to ask you something.

39
00:01:07,360 --> 00:01:08,950
Have the tenants from rooms 202,

40
00:01:09,340 --> 00:01:10,150
204,

41
00:01:10,320 --> 00:01:11,180
308,

42
00:01:11,350 --> 00:01:12,100
and 407

43
00:01:12,420 --> 00:01:13,440
come back to their rooms?

44
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:14,250
Oh,

45
00:01:14,700 --> 00:01:17,350
I think Mr. Duong from room 204

46
00:01:17,770 --> 00:01:19,450
- is in his room today.
- That's right.

47
00:01:19,450 --> 00:01:20,240
He is?

48
00:01:20,240 --> 00:01:20,680
- Yes.
- Yes.

49
00:01:20,680 --> 00:01:21,380
Hey,

50
00:01:21,380 --> 00:01:23,220
shall we go talk to him in room 204?

51
00:01:23,220 --> 00:01:23,850
Yeah, alright.

52
00:01:24,740 --> 00:01:25,460
Dobby,

53
00:01:26,120 --> 00:01:28,039
What outfit did you burn for me?!

54
00:01:28,039 --> 00:01:28,800
Huh?!

55
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:30,180
I am not a turtle.

56
00:01:31,090 --> 00:01:31,750
Hey,

57
00:01:31,750 --> 00:01:33,300
is our dorm near a canal?

58
00:01:33,890 --> 00:01:36,000
I think I saw a turtle
walking around here yesterday.

59
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:36,550
Huh?!

60
00:01:38,330 --> 00:01:40,600
Our dorm isn't close to any
canals, though.

61
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:42,550
Then it might be one of the tenants' pets.

62
00:01:42,550 --> 00:01:44,220
Can you describe its appearance

63
00:01:44,220 --> 00:01:44,950
to me?

64
00:01:45,720 --> 00:01:47,920
This turtle...is so old!

65
00:01:48,550 --> 00:01:49,220
Old turtle...

66
00:01:49,220 --> 00:01:50,289
But he acts like a child.

67
00:01:50,810 --> 00:01:51,700
One more thing,

68
00:01:51,700 --> 00:01:53,479
he's a coward

69
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:55,170
who likes to hide in his shell.

70
00:01:56,060 --> 00:01:57,320
And won't accept the truth.

71
00:01:57,320 --> 00:01:58,150
Hey,

72
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:01,340
are you talking about an actual turtle?
Or are you insulting someone?

73
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:02,040
Right?

74
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:03,320
Of course I'm talking about a turtle.

75
00:02:03,850 --> 00:02:04,820
Who else would I insult?

76
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:05,970
Why?

77
00:02:06,440 --> 00:02:07,750
Is there anyone who looks
like a turtle around here?

78
00:02:08,650 --> 00:02:09,530
I see.

79
00:02:09,530 --> 00:02:10,320
There is no one else.

80
00:02:10,320 --> 00:02:10,960
You are talking about me.

81
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:12,550
Dobby,

82
00:02:12,930 --> 00:02:14,170
what did I even do to you?

83
00:02:14,170 --> 00:02:14,560
Huh?

84
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:15,500
Why are you insulting me?!

85
00:02:16,650 --> 00:02:18,980
Come on, let's go to room 204.

86
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:19,750
Okay.

87
00:02:20,020 --> 00:02:21,570
Hey, answer me... Hey!

88
00:02:21,570 --> 00:02:23,600
♫Ho-hi...♫

89
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:24,380
Dobby!

90
00:02:26,490 --> 00:02:27,450
You got rejected.

91
00:02:29,160 --> 00:02:36,970
♫The D Dorm, meet me at the D Dorm♫

92
00:02:38,990 --> 00:02:45,910
♫Every step we take has a meaning♫

93
00:02:45,910 --> 00:02:51,810
♫No path is ever meaningless♫

94
00:02:53,320 --> 00:02:59,640
♫As long as our hearts keep searching♫

95
00:03:00,340 --> 00:03:04,910
♫One day, we'll find
what we're yearning for♫

96
00:03:04,910 --> 00:03:08,560
♫Walking alone is fine,
but it's better when you're by my side♫

97
00:03:08,560 --> 00:03:12,150
♫It won't be lonely
when you're here to walk beside♫

98
00:03:12,150 --> 00:03:15,070
♫Like a love that waits, waits at the D Dorm♫

99
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:17,910
♫Like a love that remains,
remains at the dorm♫

100
00:03:17,930 --> 00:03:25,100
♫Meaningful love and good things
await on every path♫

101
00:03:25,100 --> 00:03:32,300
♫It might not be a coincidence
that we get to meet♫

102
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:39,500
♫There might be hidden meanings
on the path beneath our feet♫

103
00:03:39,500 --> 00:03:46,700
♫Perhaps the D Dorm
is what led me to meet you♫

104
00:03:46,700 --> 00:03:50,490
[The D Dorm]

105
00:03:50,570 --> 00:03:51,370
Mm...

106
00:03:51,370 --> 00:03:52,460
I think this room has the potential.

107
00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:53,970
Ow!

108
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:54,550
- Oh?
- Whoa...

109
00:03:55,290 --> 00:03:55,750
Ouch...

110
00:03:56,320 --> 00:03:57,290
I'm sorry.

111
00:04:06,210 --> 00:04:09,080
[Duong, occupation: stock trader]

112
00:04:09,210 --> 00:04:10,660
Are you hurt?

113
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:11,350
Oh?

114
00:04:11,890 --> 00:04:13,580
Are you Mr. Duong from room 204?

115
00:04:13,880 --> 00:04:14,950
Oh...right.

116
00:04:14,950 --> 00:04:15,610
What is it to you?

117
00:04:15,960 --> 00:04:16,600
Huh?

118
00:04:16,820 --> 00:04:17,880
Does it look like
steamed or fried taro?

119
00:04:18,250 --> 00:04:18,769
Then...

120
00:04:19,170 --> 00:04:20,290
buy me fried taro.

121
00:04:20,290 --> 00:04:22,019
- Oh...
- I see...

122
00:04:22,019 --> 00:04:23,540
- He's on the phone.
- He is, isn't he?

123
00:04:25,010 --> 00:04:25,750
I'm sorry about earlier.

124
00:04:26,050 --> 00:04:27,450
You bumped into me, right?

125
00:04:27,450 --> 00:04:28,600
Give me 2,000 baht.

126
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:29,200
Huh?!

127
00:04:29,200 --> 00:04:29,700
What?

128
00:04:29,880 --> 00:04:31,170
Why do I have to pay you?

129
00:04:31,170 --> 00:04:32,680
Well, you bumped into me.
And it hurt.

130
00:04:32,810 --> 00:04:34,040
You also wasted my time.

131
00:04:34,150 --> 00:04:37,050
Most importantly, you made me
look away from the stock charts.

132
00:04:37,050 --> 00:04:38,460
I could lose hundreds
of thousands of baht

133
00:04:38,760 --> 00:04:40,460
in just a few seconds.

134
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:41,350
Whoa...

135
00:04:41,700 --> 00:04:43,100
What? I'm not paying!

136
00:04:43,100 --> 00:04:44,810
Then work to repay me.

137
00:04:44,950 --> 00:04:45,960
Go put up these flyers.

138
00:04:46,490 --> 00:04:46,940
Huh?

139
00:04:46,940 --> 00:04:47,350
Hey...

140
00:04:47,780 --> 00:04:48,550
Hey,

141
00:04:49,010 --> 00:04:51,420
when you want someone
to do something for you, ask nicely.

142
00:04:51,420 --> 00:04:53,010
Who would want to help
if you talk like that?

143
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:54,040
Yeah.

144
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:55,960
If you can find my bird,
I'll give you 5,000 baht.

145
00:04:55,960 --> 00:04:56,490
Ooh!

146
00:04:56,950 --> 00:04:58,150
Wow, even faster than me.

147
00:04:58,420 --> 00:04:59,560
I'll put them up all over our dorm.

148
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:00,320
Hey,

149
00:05:00,690 --> 00:05:02,140
since you're here,

150
00:05:02,140 --> 00:05:04,890
do you happen to have
a relative named Gaysorn?

151
00:05:04,890 --> 00:05:05,540
Missed gain.

152
00:05:05,540 --> 00:05:06,550
Huh?!

153
00:05:06,680 --> 00:05:08,100
Grandma Gaysorn sells grains?

154
00:05:08,100 --> 00:05:08,820
Buy the dip.

155
00:05:08,820 --> 00:05:10,650
So, does she sell grains or dips?

156
00:05:10,650 --> 00:05:11,610
Sell it to your father!

157
00:05:11,610 --> 00:05:12,360
Hey!

158
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:13,640
- You're gonna get...
- Whoa, whoa.

159
00:05:13,640 --> 00:05:14,780
Hey, calm down. What's wrong?

160
00:05:14,780 --> 00:05:16,720
- Wait, wait, wait.
- He insulted us.

161
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:17,780
He wasn't.

162
00:05:17,780 --> 00:05:18,810
He's on the phone.

163
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:20,770
I told you to sell it to your father.

164
00:05:20,770 --> 00:05:22,490
- He likes that stock, doesn't he?
- Oh.

165
00:05:22,490 --> 00:05:23,600
Grains...

166
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:25,480
What a waste of my time.

167
00:05:25,480 --> 00:05:26,610
You're talking on the phone, right?

168
00:05:26,610 --> 00:05:27,780
I'm talking to you all.

169
00:05:27,780 --> 00:05:28,760
- Huh?
- What?!

170
00:05:28,760 --> 00:05:29,200
What?

171
00:05:29,200 --> 00:05:31,160
How could you say that?!

172
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:32,950
It seems like...

173
00:05:33,690 --> 00:05:35,800
he won't waste
his time talking to us.

174
00:05:37,320 --> 00:05:38,280
Guard Dum, can I see that?

175
00:05:38,280 --> 00:05:38,950
What's this?

176
00:05:40,150 --> 00:05:42,860
"Missing Bird: Duidui.

177
00:05:42,860 --> 00:05:44,400
A reward of 5,000 baht.

178
00:05:44,580 --> 00:05:46,150
Find it, get paid."

179
00:05:46,620 --> 00:05:48,250
Dobby, how about this?

180
00:05:48,659 --> 00:05:50,810
You help him look for his bird

181
00:05:50,810 --> 00:05:52,460
to win him over.

182
00:05:52,460 --> 00:05:53,810
That way, he will talk to you.

183
00:05:54,340 --> 00:05:55,750
Everyone, how about this?

184
00:05:57,180 --> 00:05:58,810
We should all look for his bird.

185
00:05:59,240 --> 00:06:01,750
Because if we help him first,
he might be willing to talk to us.

186
00:06:02,950 --> 00:06:04,900
See? My idea...

187
00:06:04,900 --> 00:06:05,890
Alright, everyone.

188
00:06:06,140 --> 00:06:07,010
What a great idea!

189
00:06:07,170 --> 00:06:08,220
We'll... Here.

190
00:06:08,410 --> 00:06:10,150
- Put it up here.
- I... My idea...

191
00:06:10,530 --> 00:06:11,240
Dobby!

192
00:06:11,240 --> 00:06:11,930
It looks perfect here.

193
00:06:11,930 --> 00:06:13,620
Do I even exist or what? Huh?

194
00:06:13,620 --> 00:06:15,120
- Here, too. Alright, Guard Dum?
- Dobby.

195
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:16,150
- Here as well.
- Yes, alright.

196
00:06:16,150 --> 00:06:16,980
Come on, follow me.

197
00:06:16,980 --> 00:06:18,590
- Come on.
- Listen to me!

198
00:06:18,610 --> 00:06:20,210
[The D Dorm]

199
00:06:20,440 --> 00:06:22,020
What's this surprise supposed to be?

200
00:06:22,020 --> 00:06:23,480
I can't wait to see it.

201
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:25,580
- Three, two, one!
- Three, two, one!

202
00:06:25,580 --> 00:06:27,900
- Surprise!
- Surprise!

203
00:06:27,900 --> 00:06:29,350
Whoa!

204
00:06:29,900 --> 00:06:32,760
Did you buy all of this for me?
It's all brand-new?

205
00:06:32,950 --> 00:06:35,350
Ooh...

206
00:06:36,010 --> 00:06:37,120
Wow!

207
00:06:37,320 --> 00:06:38,260
Amazing.

208
00:06:38,260 --> 00:06:39,780
Where did you get the money from?

209
00:06:39,780 --> 00:06:41,120
I used the savings, Mom.

210
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:43,750
Oh, how sweet of you...

211
00:06:45,810 --> 00:06:48,040
Aw...

212
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:50,280
You didn't have to
use the money you saved.

213
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:51,640
It's alright, Mom.

214
00:06:51,640 --> 00:06:53,000
Cause the money we used

215
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:54,060
came from your room.

216
00:06:54,890 --> 00:06:55,540
Here.

217
00:06:58,150 --> 00:06:59,220
Hey, Dollar.

218
00:06:59,220 --> 00:07:00,550
Are you a cop or a thief, huh?

219
00:07:00,960 --> 00:07:02,370
Hey, Mom...

220
00:07:02,370 --> 00:07:03,200
We're only borrowing.

221
00:07:03,200 --> 00:07:05,580
We'll pay you back after we get paid.

222
00:07:05,580 --> 00:07:07,180
Don't you think we should redecorate a little

223
00:07:07,180 --> 00:07:08,950
for our restaurant's grand reopening?

224
00:07:08,950 --> 00:07:09,690
That's right, Mom.

225
00:07:09,690 --> 00:07:11,220
Aw, it's okay.

226
00:07:16,150 --> 00:07:17,570
Yes, Pha?

227
00:07:18,410 --> 00:07:19,040
Oh.

228
00:07:19,220 --> 00:07:21,220
Alright, one moment.

229
00:07:21,720 --> 00:07:22,480
- Mom,
- Hm?

230
00:07:22,480 --> 00:07:25,300
Pha called me to tell me that
the cook on set is sick,

231
00:07:25,610 --> 00:07:27,160
so they asked if you could go instead?

232
00:07:27,160 --> 00:07:28,760
I can't. It's too sudden.

233
00:07:28,760 --> 00:07:30,010
Our shop isn't ready yet.

234
00:07:30,010 --> 00:07:31,080
- Dollar isn't free, either.
- Mm.

235
00:07:31,080 --> 00:07:32,250
I can't do it alone.

236
00:07:32,250 --> 00:07:33,800
But they said they'll give
us 15,000 baht.

237
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:35,060
- Then what are we waiting for?
- Whoa.

238
00:07:35,210 --> 00:07:37,010
Well, money talks, honey.

239
00:07:37,010 --> 00:07:38,400
Come on, Dollar!

240
00:07:38,400 --> 00:07:39,250
Carry the gas tank.

241
00:07:39,250 --> 00:07:40,000
Alright, Mom. Let's...

242
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,100
Hello, Pha?

243
00:07:41,100 --> 00:07:42,810
- My mother... My family
- Dollar!

244
00:07:42,810 --> 00:07:43,260
will go right away.

245
00:07:43,260 --> 00:07:44,770
- I'm not a gas tank.
- Oh?

246
00:07:44,950 --> 00:07:45,960
- Mm.
- Sorry, Mom.

247
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:47,350
- Take our things to the car.
- Okay, Pha.

248
00:07:47,460 --> 00:07:48,040
- Let's go.
- Hurry, Mom.

249
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:49,750
- Mom...
- Let's go to the market first.

250
00:07:53,010 --> 00:07:53,530
Woo!

251
00:07:53,810 --> 00:07:54,800
What are you doing?!

252
00:07:55,080 --> 00:07:55,750
Woo!

253
00:07:57,300 --> 00:07:58,150
Duidui,

254
00:07:58,150 --> 00:07:59,020
where are you?

255
00:07:59,020 --> 00:08:00,340
Come out.

256
00:08:00,340 --> 00:08:02,440
We have sweet and delicious
sunflower seeds for you.

257
00:08:02,440 --> 00:08:03,260
Come eat some.

258
00:08:03,770 --> 00:08:04,650
Come, Duidui.

259
00:08:05,210 --> 00:08:06,140
Ugh!

260
00:08:06,140 --> 00:08:07,690
What are you doing?

261
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:09,980
Perhaps we're catching fish.

262
00:08:09,980 --> 00:08:10,780
- Oh.
- Hm?

263
00:08:10,780 --> 00:08:12,200
We're all dressed up like this

264
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:13,890
to look for a parrot.

265
00:08:13,890 --> 00:08:15,730
Hey, I'm giving it my all.

266
00:08:15,730 --> 00:08:16,760
I can only hope...

267
00:08:17,010 --> 00:08:18,820
that Gramps will find that 5,000 baht.

268
00:08:18,820 --> 00:08:19,440
Hm?

269
00:08:19,750 --> 00:08:20,400
What 5,000?

270
00:08:20,840 --> 00:08:23,180
Oh, I mean Grandma Gaysorn.

271
00:08:23,180 --> 00:08:24,260
The words sound alike.

272
00:08:24,550 --> 00:08:25,530
Not even close.

273
00:08:25,530 --> 00:08:27,720
Your outfits don't look like birds at all.

274
00:08:27,720 --> 00:08:29,350
More like you're performing a ritual dance.

275
00:08:29,350 --> 00:08:30,090
Hey!

276
00:08:30,090 --> 00:08:31,880
And the bird flew off
a long time ago,

277
00:08:31,880 --> 00:08:33,370
so it won't be coming back
around here.

278
00:08:33,370 --> 00:08:34,150
Hey, Ms. Danis,

279
00:08:34,419 --> 00:08:36,780
I saw the bird flying around here earlier.

280
00:08:37,039 --> 00:08:38,950
I tried to catch it, but I failed.

281
00:08:39,220 --> 00:08:39,730
Hey.

282
00:08:39,960 --> 00:08:41,770
But didn't you say
you were going to see the director?

283
00:08:42,010 --> 00:08:42,809
Why are you here?

284
00:08:43,080 --> 00:08:44,450
I was going to.

285
00:08:44,450 --> 00:08:45,610
I thought I saw two crazy people,

286
00:08:46,660 --> 00:08:48,330
so I came here to help you out.

287
00:08:48,330 --> 00:08:50,360
I didn't think you'd be one of them, too.

288
00:08:51,090 --> 00:08:51,660
Is that so?

289
00:08:51,690 --> 00:08:52,640
- Yeah...
- Oh, there you are, Duidui.

290
00:08:52,640 --> 00:08:54,000
- Duidui!
- Duidui!

291
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:54,550
Duidui!

292
00:08:54,550 --> 00:08:56,050
- Duidui, my foot!
- Duidui...

293
00:08:56,380 --> 00:08:57,260
I'm leaving.

294
00:08:58,150 --> 00:08:59,970
We won't catch the bird
because you're too loud.

295
00:08:59,970 --> 00:09:00,810
Ugh...

296
00:09:02,120 --> 00:09:02,610
What?

297
00:09:02,610 --> 00:09:03,360
Mr. Dobby.

298
00:09:03,860 --> 00:09:04,660
- Whoa.
- That's...

299
00:09:04,850 --> 00:09:05,350
Is that...

300
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:08,950
Maybe the parrot came
down to eat the seeds?

301
00:09:09,530 --> 00:09:10,460
That means it worked.

302
00:09:10,460 --> 00:09:11,350
Come on.

303
00:09:12,210 --> 00:09:13,260
- Come on.
- Get in there.

304
00:09:13,750 --> 00:09:14,810
Three...

305
00:09:21,220 --> 00:09:21,780
Got you.

306
00:09:24,310 --> 00:09:25,190
Hey!

307
00:09:26,010 --> 00:09:26,950
Oh, Mr. Dawin?

308
00:09:27,220 --> 00:09:28,150
What are you doing here?

309
00:09:28,150 --> 00:09:29,760
I was hiding to catch the bird,

310
00:09:30,420 --> 00:09:32,060
but I think I stepped on an ant nest.

311
00:09:32,060 --> 00:09:32,460
Ugh...

312
00:09:32,950 --> 00:09:34,150
You're short on money too, huh?

313
00:09:34,150 --> 00:09:35,770
I don't really care about that 5,000 baht.

314
00:09:36,250 --> 00:09:38,020
I only care about your five fingers.

315
00:09:38,020 --> 00:09:38,570
Give it to me.

316
00:09:38,570 --> 00:09:39,560
Whoa, whoa!

317
00:09:42,180 --> 00:09:43,750
I made a deal with Guard Dum.

318
00:09:44,040 --> 00:09:45,580
If I can catch the bird,

319
00:09:45,580 --> 00:09:46,780
he'll take the money.

320
00:09:47,140 --> 00:09:48,550
And I get to hold your hand.

321
00:09:48,980 --> 00:09:50,360
He can't worm his way out of this one

322
00:09:50,500 --> 00:09:53,210
because we made a contract!

323
00:09:53,780 --> 00:09:54,550
He's cautious.

324
00:09:56,060 --> 00:09:57,420
How dare you sell

325
00:09:57,780 --> 00:09:59,640
your beloved brother out like this?!

326
00:10:00,140 --> 00:10:00,760
Hey!

327
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:02,400
Help me find Duidui first.

328
00:10:02,660 --> 00:10:03,760
You can deal with him later.

329
00:10:04,150 --> 00:10:06,550
Is this the parrot you're looking for?

330
00:10:08,180 --> 00:10:08,950
- Huh?
- Huh?

331
00:10:09,140 --> 00:10:10,150
- Duidui!
- Duidui!

332
00:10:10,380 --> 00:10:11,960
I was lifting this barbell,

333
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:13,120
and it landed on my shoulder.

334
00:10:13,400 --> 00:10:14,570
Can someone come take it away?

335
00:10:14,810 --> 00:10:16,480
The weight is unbalanced.
My muscles might end up uneven.

336
00:10:18,220 --> 00:10:18,780
Go, go, go.

337
00:10:19,210 --> 00:10:19,640
Hurry.

338
00:10:19,640 --> 00:10:20,780
Don't move around too much.

339
00:10:22,890 --> 00:10:23,610
Don't move.

340
00:10:23,890 --> 00:10:24,550
Stay still.

341
00:10:27,650 --> 00:10:28,410
Dolly,

342
00:10:28,640 --> 00:10:31,040
have you finished making
the fried minced pork balls?

343
00:10:31,040 --> 00:10:32,040
Yes...

344
00:10:32,040 --> 00:10:33,060
Are you done?

345
00:10:33,060 --> 00:10:34,150
Anyway...

346
00:10:34,420 --> 00:10:35,610
take care, alright?

347
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:37,380
If you want to eat something,
just tell me.

348
00:10:37,530 --> 00:10:39,490
I'll ask Mom to make it for you.

349
00:10:40,300 --> 00:10:42,200
I hope your legs get better soon.

350
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:44,950
I'll hang up now, Mr. Drip.

351
00:10:45,210 --> 00:10:46,600
I have to get back to work.

352
00:10:47,640 --> 00:10:48,550
Dolly!

353
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:49,750
Oh?

354
00:10:50,050 --> 00:10:50,650
What is it?

355
00:10:50,650 --> 00:10:52,760
I said, have you finished making the pork?

356
00:10:54,250 --> 00:10:55,120
Look.

357
00:10:55,120 --> 00:10:57,320
I've been making them
since this morning.

358
00:10:58,320 --> 00:10:59,350
Whoa!

359
00:10:59,900 --> 00:11:00,770
Heart-shaped?

360
00:11:00,940 --> 00:11:01,640
How creative.

361
00:11:01,640 --> 00:11:02,170
What?

362
00:11:02,170 --> 00:11:02,800
Hmph,

363
00:11:02,800 --> 00:11:03,800
how imaginative.

364
00:11:03,800 --> 00:11:05,240
You put in so much effort.

365
00:11:05,240 --> 00:11:06,550
Oh, Mom...

366
00:11:06,550 --> 00:11:08,570
we have to switch things up
from time to time,

367
00:11:08,570 --> 00:11:10,020
so it won't be boring.

368
00:11:10,020 --> 00:11:11,040
That's enough.

369
00:11:11,040 --> 00:11:12,100
I'll do it myself.

370
00:11:12,100 --> 00:11:13,200
- Mom.
- You're so slow.

371
00:11:13,370 --> 00:11:14,040
- Hey...
- Oh?

372
00:11:14,420 --> 00:11:17,130
I told you to throw this bag
of meatballs away this morning.

373
00:11:17,350 --> 00:11:18,550
It's already gone bad. Understand?

374
00:11:18,680 --> 00:11:19,250
Yes.

375
00:11:19,530 --> 00:11:20,080
Ugh...

376
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:22,370
Stop wasting your time
shaping these into hearts.

377
00:11:22,770 --> 00:11:25,290
The crew can eat
meatballs in any shape just fine.

378
00:11:25,290 --> 00:11:26,950
- Roll it like this, then off it goes.
- Okay.

379
00:11:27,770 --> 00:11:29,180
- Like this, see?
- Mm.

380
00:11:29,350 --> 00:11:30,280
- Whoa!
- Whoa!

381
00:11:30,280 --> 00:11:32,220
- Come here!
- Whoa, whoa, what?

382
00:11:32,220 --> 00:11:34,150
I heard there's a lot of good food here.

383
00:11:34,300 --> 00:11:34,960
So why don't you...

384
00:11:34,960 --> 00:11:35,350
Serve!

385
00:11:35,490 --> 00:11:35,800
Serve!

386
00:11:35,800 --> 00:11:37,750
Serve me a dish?

387
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:44,950
[Dim, occupation: extra]

388
00:11:45,680 --> 00:11:46,570
Hello, Granny.

389
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:50,080
If you weren't so sweet-looking,
I'd be angry.

390
00:11:50,300 --> 00:11:51,420
Oh, wait, wait, wait.

391
00:11:51,420 --> 00:11:52,410
- Calm down.
- I'm sorry.

392
00:11:52,610 --> 00:11:54,550
Think of that as him
practicing his lines before filming.

393
00:11:54,550 --> 00:11:56,210
Whoa...

394
00:11:56,210 --> 00:11:57,800
Stop being so aggressive for now.

395
00:11:57,940 --> 00:12:00,220
Don't lose focus so easily, understand?

396
00:12:00,220 --> 00:12:01,900
When you're acting off script,

397
00:12:01,900 --> 00:12:03,440
you have to stay in character.

398
00:12:03,440 --> 00:12:04,570
Stay in character.

399
00:12:04,570 --> 00:12:05,160
Understood?

400
00:12:05,520 --> 00:12:06,900
- Yes.
- Good.

401
00:12:06,900 --> 00:12:09,100
I can't believe
you can actually be this sensible.

402
00:12:09,940 --> 00:12:10,980
When he's at the dorm...

403
00:12:10,980 --> 00:12:11,350
Yeah?

404
00:12:11,460 --> 00:12:12,360
He's silly

405
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:13,420
and goofy.

406
00:12:13,420 --> 00:12:15,560
Pa dum, dum. Pa ding, ding, ding.

407
00:12:15,560 --> 00:12:16,970
Doodle, doodle, doodle doo.

408
00:12:16,970 --> 00:12:19,240
Tootle ootle ootle, tootle ti toot...

409
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:20,480
- Hey!
- Whoa!

410
00:12:20,690 --> 00:12:22,150
You're not that different from him.

411
00:12:23,170 --> 00:12:23,780
Auntie,

412
00:12:23,780 --> 00:12:25,290
is there anything to eat?
I'm so hungry.

413
00:12:25,290 --> 00:12:26,570
Oh, the rice hasn't even finished cooking.

414
00:12:26,570 --> 00:12:28,720
Where am I supposed to get energy from?!

415
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:32,010
I'll snack on these for now.

416
00:12:32,290 --> 00:12:33,160
Don't!

417
00:12:33,160 --> 00:12:33,810
Ow.

418
00:12:33,810 --> 00:12:35,620
There won't be
enough food to go with the rice.

419
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:38,160
Dolly, Dodo has arrived on set.

420
00:12:38,340 --> 00:12:39,610
Come help him get dressed right away.

421
00:12:41,210 --> 00:12:42,040
Okay.

422
00:12:42,810 --> 00:12:44,620
Mom, Dodo's here. Hurry up, okay?

423
00:12:44,780 --> 00:12:46,940
Why didn't you turn on the stove?

424
00:12:47,140 --> 00:12:47,890
Can you turn up the heat?

425
00:12:48,160 --> 00:12:49,620
They're calling you. Go.

426
00:12:49,620 --> 00:12:51,140
Yes, I'm on my way.

427
00:12:52,620 --> 00:12:53,570
This will have to do.

428
00:12:53,770 --> 00:12:54,550
Auntie, I'll be taking this.

429
00:12:54,780 --> 00:12:56,220
I said no.

430
00:12:56,220 --> 00:12:57,600
The proportions are going to be off.

431
00:12:58,360 --> 00:12:59,710
What did he even take?

432
00:13:07,750 --> 00:13:08,820
Let's rehearse one more time.

433
00:13:08,820 --> 00:13:09,450
Okay.

434
00:13:09,640 --> 00:13:10,370
Action.

435
00:13:11,650 --> 00:13:14,400
This simple food
isn't fit for Captain Salween!

436
00:13:14,400 --> 00:13:15,650
What ween? That's a river.

437
00:13:16,280 --> 00:13:16,860
Try again.

438
00:13:16,860 --> 00:13:17,800
Captain Sala Song!

439
00:13:17,800 --> 00:13:18,370
That's a temple!

440
00:13:19,770 --> 00:13:20,790
Captain Sinful!

441
00:13:20,950 --> 00:13:21,770
Ugh!

442
00:13:21,970 --> 00:13:23,120
It's Sarasin!

443
00:13:23,240 --> 00:13:24,550
The protagonist is "Sarasin."

444
00:13:24,690 --> 00:13:26,000
Try to focus.

445
00:13:26,280 --> 00:13:26,950
Are you alright?

446
00:13:27,450 --> 00:13:29,120
Well, I'm nervous...

447
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:31,570
I have to act in a scene with
my celebrity crush.

448
00:13:31,570 --> 00:13:33,440
I'm already too flustered.

449
00:13:33,580 --> 00:13:35,350
I'm squealing!

450
00:13:35,970 --> 00:13:36,890
I'll try to calm down.

451
00:13:36,890 --> 00:13:37,240
Mm.

452
00:13:37,420 --> 00:13:38,170
Okay...

453
00:13:58,570 --> 00:14:01,480
[Dodo, occupation: actor]

454
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:02,810
Mr. Dodo...

455
00:14:04,440 --> 00:14:05,350
Can you let go now?

456
00:14:05,370 --> 00:14:06,010
Oops.

457
00:14:06,360 --> 00:14:07,210
I'm sorry.

458
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:07,980
Come here.

459
00:14:08,800 --> 00:14:10,730
- Dodo, hello.
- Hello.

460
00:14:10,730 --> 00:14:11,780
Are you alright?

461
00:14:11,890 --> 00:14:12,550
I'm fine.

462
00:14:12,740 --> 00:14:14,130
Have you started filming?

463
00:14:14,130 --> 00:14:15,810
Uh, while we were waiting for you,

464
00:14:15,810 --> 00:14:17,170
we filmed a few scenes.

465
00:14:17,170 --> 00:14:18,880
We'll finish those up,

466
00:14:18,880 --> 00:14:20,330
then we'll film yours, alright?

467
00:14:20,330 --> 00:14:21,930
Oh...so you're implying that

468
00:14:22,280 --> 00:14:23,800
I wasted your time?

469
00:14:23,800 --> 00:14:24,550
Oops.

470
00:14:24,810 --> 00:14:26,000
Then go ahead and replace the lead actor.

471
00:14:26,240 --> 00:14:27,610
Uh... Wait, wait, wait, Dodo.

472
00:14:27,610 --> 00:14:28,770
Calm down, okay?

473
00:14:28,770 --> 00:14:31,180
Who would dare say that to you?

474
00:14:31,180 --> 00:14:32,300
No need to change the lead actor.

475
00:14:32,300 --> 00:14:34,150
I'll change the schedule for you.

476
00:14:34,150 --> 00:14:35,350
Alright, stop everything

477
00:14:35,350 --> 00:14:36,220
and film Dodo's scenes first.

478
00:14:36,220 --> 00:14:37,060
Okay, tell the crew.

479
00:14:37,060 --> 00:14:38,400
Hey, stop everything. Come on.

480
00:14:39,320 --> 00:14:40,040
Director,

481
00:14:40,040 --> 00:14:41,530
- Yes?
- when will we get to have lunch, then?

482
00:14:41,730 --> 00:14:42,360
Who is this?

483
00:14:42,940 --> 00:14:43,750
Oh...

484
00:14:44,100 --> 00:14:44,720
Who?

485
00:14:46,040 --> 00:14:47,140
I'm a supporting actor.

486
00:14:47,350 --> 00:14:48,100
Oh...

487
00:14:48,100 --> 00:14:50,120
He'll be supporting you in the scene.

488
00:14:50,120 --> 00:14:50,950
Hello.

489
00:14:51,690 --> 00:14:53,700
If he's hungry, let him eat.

490
00:14:54,550 --> 00:14:55,750
- Wow, thank you so much.
- How kind.

491
00:14:55,750 --> 00:14:56,950
We'll find a replacement.

492
00:14:56,950 --> 00:14:57,620
I'm in a rush here.

493
00:14:57,800 --> 00:14:58,570
- Whoa.
- Hey.

494
00:14:58,970 --> 00:14:59,540
Just hold out a little longer.

495
00:14:59,540 --> 00:15:00,380
- Dodo.
- Yes.

496
00:15:00,540 --> 00:15:01,750
Dodo!

497
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:06,930
That is your celebrity crush?

498
00:15:06,930 --> 00:15:08,130
That's a villain.

499
00:15:08,620 --> 00:15:11,040
How could I know he'd act like that?

500
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:13,750
It's a good thing I ate
some fermented pork balls earlier.

501
00:15:14,400 --> 00:15:14,950
Hm?

502
00:15:17,060 --> 00:15:17,780
Fermented pork?

503
00:15:17,900 --> 00:15:19,750
Well, it was sour,
so I figured it was fermented pork.

504
00:15:23,700 --> 00:15:25,140
[The D Dorm]

505
00:15:25,140 --> 00:15:25,930
Mr. Duong,

506
00:15:25,930 --> 00:15:28,760
you can check if this
is the bird you're looking for.

507
00:15:29,090 --> 00:15:31,020
We can talk about the reward later.

508
00:15:31,020 --> 00:15:31,900
Tell that to your mother.

509
00:15:33,060 --> 00:15:34,900
I already told you not to
let her buy that stock.

510
00:15:35,020 --> 00:15:36,440
It's too risky.

511
00:15:36,550 --> 00:15:37,610
What did you say again?

512
00:15:37,890 --> 00:15:38,650
Oh,

513
00:15:38,650 --> 00:15:39,810
it's my mother's business.

514
00:15:40,420 --> 00:15:41,620
Anyway, let's go see the bird.

515
00:15:41,620 --> 00:15:43,080
Let's go, Mr. Duong.

516
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:44,140
Here we are.

517
00:15:44,620 --> 00:15:45,400
Is this your bird?

518
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:47,350
Duidui!

519
00:15:48,170 --> 00:15:49,320
My dear Duidui.

520
00:15:51,820 --> 00:15:52,420
Oh?

521
00:15:54,370 --> 00:15:55,750
Why is my bird so still?

522
00:15:58,890 --> 00:16:00,180
Who killed my bird?!

523
00:16:00,180 --> 00:16:00,780
Huh?!

524
00:16:07,600 --> 00:16:08,260
What?

525
00:16:08,950 --> 00:16:10,150
Why is it dead?

526
00:16:10,940 --> 00:16:11,690
Guard Dum?

527
00:16:11,880 --> 00:16:12,550
Handyman Daeng?

528
00:16:12,550 --> 00:16:13,490
What happened?!

529
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:16,900
Hey,

530
00:16:16,900 --> 00:16:18,050
why are you all quiet?

531
00:16:19,100 --> 00:16:21,290
Day and I love this bird like our own child.

532
00:16:21,290 --> 00:16:22,880
Whoever did this, bring me 50,000 baht.

533
00:16:22,880 --> 00:16:23,780
Huh?!

534
00:16:25,750 --> 00:16:26,620
50,000?!

535
00:16:27,130 --> 00:16:28,700
Mr. Dobby killed your bird.

536
00:16:28,700 --> 00:16:29,350
Oh...

537
00:16:29,540 --> 00:16:30,170
Huh?!

538
00:16:30,960 --> 00:16:31,750
Mr. Dobby...

539
00:16:34,660 --> 00:16:35,570
I saw it with my own two eyes.

540
00:16:38,780 --> 00:16:39,930
♫Who wants to be rich?♫

541
00:16:39,930 --> 00:16:41,350
♫I do, I do♫

542
00:16:41,350 --> 00:16:42,550
♫Who wants five thousand baht?♫

543
00:16:42,550 --> 00:16:44,260
♫I do, I do♫

544
00:16:44,950 --> 00:16:46,480
How lucky.

545
00:16:46,480 --> 00:16:48,440
Let's feed Duidui.

546
00:16:48,440 --> 00:16:50,620
Shut the hell up, you foul-mouthed bird!

547
00:16:51,200 --> 00:16:52,420
Little Eggy.

548
00:16:52,600 --> 00:16:53,760
Little Eggy.

549
00:16:53,980 --> 00:16:55,140
Little Eggy.

550
00:16:55,330 --> 00:16:56,420
Little Eggy.

551
00:16:57,380 --> 00:16:59,540
Who taught you to call me that?

552
00:17:00,050 --> 00:17:00,550
Shut up!

553
00:17:00,690 --> 00:17:01,750
Little Eggy.

554
00:17:02,090 --> 00:17:03,170
Little Eggy.

555
00:17:03,290 --> 00:17:04,940
Do you have a death wish?

556
00:17:05,349 --> 00:17:05,819
Huh?

557
00:17:06,020 --> 00:17:07,130
You want this, right?

558
00:17:07,290 --> 00:17:08,450
