00:26:14,420 --> 00:26:16,570
- Dollar has a great body.
- Dollar has a great body.

843
00:26:17,680 --> 00:26:18,890
Yes, "Dollar has a great body."

844
00:26:20,010 --> 00:26:21,290
That's what happened.

845
00:26:22,260 --> 00:26:23,350
I didn't kill Duidui.

846
00:26:25,010 --> 00:26:26,610
Then who did?

847
00:26:27,690 --> 00:26:28,520
Come to think of it...

848
00:26:28,740 --> 00:26:29,780
I'm suspicious of someone.

849
00:26:30,200 --> 00:26:31,750
He might be Duidui's killer.

850
00:26:32,220 --> 00:26:32,950
This person

851
00:26:33,460 --> 00:26:34,770
normally puts on

852
00:26:36,300 --> 00:26:38,200
a kind and caring front.

853
00:26:38,410 --> 00:26:38,950
Hm?

854
00:26:39,440 --> 00:26:39,970
Who?

855
00:26:41,090 --> 00:26:41,810
But today,

856
00:26:42,050 --> 00:26:43,750
I saw his cruel side.

857
00:26:45,250 --> 00:26:45,940
Handyman Daeng!

858
00:26:45,940 --> 00:26:46,960
Hm? Yes?

859
00:26:51,320 --> 00:26:52,040
Whoa?!

860
00:26:52,040 --> 00:26:52,800
It's not me.

861
00:26:53,350 --> 00:26:54,340
I didn't kill it!

862
00:26:59,530 --> 00:27:00,970
Do you feel better, Dim?

863
00:27:02,050 --> 00:27:02,580
Wow...

864
00:27:02,820 --> 00:27:03,970
What kind of film set

865
00:27:04,340 --> 00:27:05,760
doesn't prepare anything

866
00:27:05,760 --> 00:27:07,220
for a chili-eating scene?

867
00:27:07,570 --> 00:27:08,950
Not even a single carton of milk.

868
00:27:09,220 --> 00:27:10,150
Come on now.

869
00:27:10,300 --> 00:27:12,550
It's not entirely the crew's fault.

870
00:27:12,940 --> 00:27:16,150
They probably didn't think
the lead actor would mess up

871
00:27:16,400 --> 00:27:17,660
such a simple scene,

872
00:27:18,100 --> 00:27:20,290
making someone eat
almost 20 chili peppers.

873
00:27:20,660 --> 00:27:21,960
It's just the spice for me.

874
00:27:22,560 --> 00:27:23,490
But I don't know if Dax

875
00:27:23,490 --> 00:27:24,850
will have the energy to keep acting.

876
00:27:24,850 --> 00:27:25,410
Ooh...

877
00:27:25,410 --> 00:27:26,210
- I can do this.
- Whoa...

878
00:27:26,210 --> 00:27:27,540
- Sit down. Sit, sit.
- Oh...

879
00:27:27,970 --> 00:27:28,720
I'm alright.

880
00:27:28,720 --> 00:27:30,330
Would you like an electrolyte drink?

881
00:27:30,330 --> 00:27:31,750
No, no, don't.

882
00:27:32,420 --> 00:27:34,340
I wouldn't be able to keep
it in my system anyway.

883
00:27:34,580 --> 00:27:35,100
Oh.

884
00:27:35,240 --> 00:27:35,930
Right now,

885
00:27:36,220 --> 00:27:37,420
I can't eat anything.

886
00:27:37,620 --> 00:27:38,820
Whatever I eat comes right out.

887
00:27:38,820 --> 00:27:39,400
Food goes in?

888
00:27:39,600 --> 00:27:40,150
It then comes out.

889
00:27:40,150 --> 00:27:41,350
- Oh.
- Oh.

890
00:27:41,350 --> 00:27:42,210
You can do this.

891
00:27:42,210 --> 00:27:43,220
Alright, everyone.

892
00:27:43,220 --> 00:27:44,840
- Let's film the next scene.
- They're calling you. Go.

893
00:27:44,840 --> 00:27:46,150
If you're ready, let's continue.

894
00:27:46,150 --> 00:27:46,970
Come, come.

895
00:27:47,000 --> 00:27:49,090
- I'll explain it to you.
- You've got this.

896
00:27:49,750 --> 00:27:50,610
Ready?

897
00:27:50,610 --> 00:27:51,400
Uh...

898
00:27:51,660 --> 00:27:53,610
This scene will be...

899
00:27:53,610 --> 00:27:55,860
Captain Sarasin fights with Yae and Kied,

900
00:27:56,530 --> 00:27:56,950
okay?

901
00:27:56,950 --> 00:27:58,150
The fight will go like this...

902
00:27:58,150 --> 00:27:59,350
Dodo will fight with Dax.

903
00:27:59,600 --> 00:28:02,760
And Dodo will punch Dax to the ground.

904
00:28:02,950 --> 00:28:03,770
Then...

905
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:04,940
Dim, right?

906
00:28:04,940 --> 00:28:06,300
Dim will join the scene...

907
00:28:06,300 --> 00:28:07,210
with this knife in his hand.

908
00:28:07,360 --> 00:28:08,760
Dim will approach Dodo from behind.

909
00:28:08,760 --> 00:28:10,150
But Dodo knows you're there,

910
00:28:10,150 --> 00:28:11,350
so he'll turn around and grab your wrist.

911
00:28:11,350 --> 00:28:12,550
Then you'll struggle back and forth,

912
00:28:12,720 --> 00:28:14,260
glaring at each other with hatred.

913
00:28:14,520 --> 00:28:15,560
That's the scene.

914
00:28:15,560 --> 00:28:16,150
Understood?

915
00:28:16,900 --> 00:28:17,770
- Okay.
- Yes.

916
00:28:17,900 --> 00:28:19,120
Why are your lips so red?

917
00:28:19,120 --> 00:28:20,040
When did you put on more lipstick?

918
00:28:21,130 --> 00:28:23,210
You've done several scenes already.
Why are you still nervous?

919
00:28:23,210 --> 00:28:23,880
Your lips look pale.

920
00:28:24,550 --> 00:28:25,040
Are you alright?

921
00:28:25,040 --> 00:28:26,020
- I'm alright.
- You two can do this, right?

922
00:28:26,020 --> 00:28:26,560
You've got this.

923
00:28:26,560 --> 00:28:27,300
You can do this.

924
00:28:27,640 --> 00:28:28,150
Okay.

925
00:28:28,150 --> 00:28:29,350
- Okay.
- Alright, go.

926
00:28:29,740 --> 00:28:30,240
Go.

927
00:28:30,240 --> 00:28:32,410
- Let's start.
- Get into your positions.

928
00:28:32,770 --> 00:28:33,570
Action!

929
00:28:35,060 --> 00:28:35,560
Hey!

930
00:28:46,410 --> 00:28:47,540
Ow...

931
00:29:01,100 --> 00:29:02,200
It's spicy.

932
00:29:02,690 --> 00:29:03,640
Hold it in.

933
00:29:04,150 --> 00:29:05,560
It will end soon.

934
00:29:05,580 --> 00:29:06,780
Hold it...

935
00:29:09,700 --> 00:29:10,660
Hold...

936
00:29:11,620 --> 00:29:12,980
It will end soon.

937
00:29:14,770 --> 00:29:15,520
I can do this...

938
00:29:17,570 --> 00:29:19,290
I can't do this anymore!

939
00:29:44,950 --> 00:29:45,780
Oh!

940
00:29:46,160 --> 00:29:47,360
The Bullet Chilli

941
00:29:47,600 --> 00:29:49,420
is going to be
The Bullet of Love at this point.

942
00:29:49,750 --> 00:29:50,250
Oh?

943
00:29:53,660 --> 00:29:54,250
Cut!

944
00:29:55,400 --> 00:29:57,140
What even was that acting?!

945
00:29:57,140 --> 00:29:59,580
You two have wasted my whole day.

946
00:30:00,400 --> 00:30:01,170
Director,

947
00:30:01,170 --> 00:30:01,940
replace them.

948
00:30:01,940 --> 00:30:02,950
I don't want to act
with them anymore.

949
00:30:04,610 --> 00:30:05,800
Dodo!

950
00:30:09,930 --> 00:30:10,780
It's not me.

951
00:30:10,780 --> 00:30:11,350
That's not true.

952
00:30:11,800 --> 00:30:12,740
My brother is innocent.

953
00:30:13,320 --> 00:30:14,280
He's a good person.

954
00:30:14,450 --> 00:30:15,570
He couldn't have killed the bird.

955
00:30:16,000 --> 00:30:16,780
I'm defending him,

956
00:30:16,980 --> 00:30:18,810
no matter what you say.

957
00:30:21,100 --> 00:30:22,730
So you are accomplices, huh?

958
00:30:22,860 --> 00:30:24,370
Then you'll have to pay me
25,000 baht each.

959
00:30:24,370 --> 00:30:25,620
Oh, you bird murderer!

960
00:30:26,040 --> 00:30:27,130
How could you do this?

961
00:30:27,370 --> 00:30:28,150
You backstabber!

962
00:30:29,000 --> 00:30:30,170
I really didn't do it.

963
00:30:30,170 --> 00:30:31,080
But I saw it with my own eyes.

964
00:30:31,080 --> 00:30:31,580
Huh?

965
00:30:32,050 --> 00:30:34,970
You have the strongest motive here.

966
00:30:35,780 --> 00:30:36,300
Whoa...

967
00:30:36,300 --> 00:30:37,050
What?

968
00:30:37,330 --> 00:30:38,020
Oh...

969
00:30:41,570 --> 00:30:44,020
I checked and unplugged
everything for you.

970
00:30:44,020 --> 00:30:45,580
Hey, Mom, don't hang up yet.

971
00:30:46,000 --> 00:30:47,140
When I was younger...

972
00:30:47,580 --> 00:30:48,800
how did you teach me to speak?

973
00:30:50,170 --> 00:30:52,370
What I do with that information
is up to me, Mom.

974
00:30:52,900 --> 00:30:53,880
Ugh, no.

975
00:30:53,880 --> 00:30:54,900
I didn't get anyone pregnant.

976
00:30:54,900 --> 00:30:56,370
I don't have a child, Mom!

977
00:30:57,220 --> 00:30:58,150
I didn't... Ugh.

978
00:30:58,290 --> 00:30:59,100
I'm hanging up.

979
00:31:00,800 --> 00:31:02,810
I can't take this anymore!

980
00:31:03,690 --> 00:31:05,350
♫The monkey holds the tiger's paw♫

981
00:31:05,610 --> 00:31:06,740
♫The tiger holds the monkey's hand♫

982
00:31:06,740 --> 00:31:09,250
I said it's annoying! Shut up!

983
00:31:09,780 --> 00:31:11,080
♫The tiger holds the monkey's hand♫

984
00:31:12,040 --> 00:31:13,130
♫The monkey holds the tiger's paw♫

985
00:31:13,130 --> 00:31:14,950
If you don't stop,

986
00:31:14,950 --> 00:31:19,210
I'll strangle you to death!

987
00:31:20,640 --> 00:31:22,210
The birdcage is placed
in front of your office.

988
00:31:22,410 --> 00:31:24,320
You couldn't stand the noise,

989
00:31:24,320 --> 00:31:25,380
so you got up

990
00:31:25,620 --> 00:31:27,800
and killed the bird out of spite.

991
00:31:29,730 --> 00:31:30,620
- Whoa...
- Hey!

992
00:31:31,240 --> 00:31:32,240
It's not like that.

993
00:31:32,450 --> 00:31:34,650
- How cruel.
- I really didn't kill Duidui.

994
00:31:34,850 --> 00:31:36,120
Did what I said

995
00:31:36,420 --> 00:31:37,500
actually happen, then?

996
00:31:37,750 --> 00:31:39,810
That...

997
00:31:42,550 --> 00:31:43,170
is true.

998
00:31:43,170 --> 00:31:44,340
- Oh?
- Oh!

999
00:31:45,330 --> 00:31:46,780
It might be true,

1000
00:31:48,100 --> 00:31:49,750
but Handyman Daeng didn't kill Duidui.

1001
00:31:50,870 --> 00:31:52,410
If you want me to back you up,

1002
00:31:52,860 --> 00:31:53,810
you know

1003
00:31:54,550 --> 00:31:55,750
what I expect in return.

1004
00:32:03,890 --> 00:32:04,660
Whoa...

1005
00:32:04,660 --> 00:32:05,170
Ugh.

1006
00:32:05,620 --> 00:32:06,290
What?

1007
00:32:07,090 --> 00:32:08,460
It's all because of you, you pervert.

1008
00:32:08,810 --> 00:32:10,680
You caused this misunderstanding.

1009
00:32:10,680 --> 00:32:11,570
What do you mean?

1010
00:32:12,550 --> 00:32:13,540
Who killed Duidui, then?

1011
00:32:13,960 --> 00:32:15,260
Nothing I said

1012
00:32:16,150 --> 00:32:17,350
was directed at Duidui,

1013
00:32:18,290 --> 00:32:18,810
but...

1014
00:32:19,380 --> 00:32:20,650
I was talking to Dawin!

1015
00:32:24,300 --> 00:32:27,980
I'll strangle you to death!

1016
00:32:27,980 --> 00:32:29,350
♫Never tired of holding hands♫

1017
00:32:29,350 --> 00:32:30,550
Please, Handyman Daeng,

1018
00:32:30,550 --> 00:32:31,750
let me hold your hand tonight.

1019
00:32:32,000 --> 00:32:33,200
I want to see ghosts.

1020
00:32:33,420 --> 00:32:34,380
Ugh,

1021
00:32:34,380 --> 00:32:36,200
you're so annoying.

1022
00:32:36,200 --> 00:32:37,060
I can't take this anymore.

1023
00:32:37,060 --> 00:32:38,170
Shut up already!

1024
00:32:38,170 --> 00:32:38,950
- Take this.
- Ow.

1025
00:32:43,340 --> 00:32:43,750
Huh?

1026
00:32:43,750 --> 00:32:45,980
All of that commotion
was you talking to Dawin...

1027
00:32:45,980 --> 00:32:46,900
and not the bird?

1028
00:32:47,610 --> 00:32:48,200
Yes.

1029
00:32:49,220 --> 00:32:49,960
Hey!

1030
00:32:50,370 --> 00:32:51,650
Will we even find out

1031
00:32:51,650 --> 00:32:53,090
who killed Duidui at this point?

1032
00:32:53,090 --> 00:32:54,930
You'll learn the truth

1033
00:32:55,750 --> 00:32:57,810
because I have evidence against the killer.

1034
00:33:00,010 --> 00:33:02,040
The murderer is in this video.

1035
00:33:03,380 --> 00:33:04,150
Good.

1036
00:33:04,780 --> 00:33:05,350
Come on,

1037
00:33:05,520 --> 00:33:06,290
let's find them.

1038
00:33:18,170 --> 00:33:20,050
Five thousand baht reward.

1039
00:33:20,340 --> 00:33:21,780
But the four of us found it
at the same time.

1040
00:33:22,300 --> 00:33:24,360
How much will each of us get?

1041
00:33:24,360 --> 00:33:26,220
Four divided by one thousand...

1042
00:33:26,600 --> 00:33:27,320
No.

1043
00:33:27,680 --> 00:33:28,770
It'd be easier if I were
the only one who found it.

1044
00:33:29,770 --> 00:33:31,400
You greedy chubby.

1045
00:33:31,750 --> 00:33:33,410
You greedy chubby.

1046
00:33:34,280 --> 00:33:35,760
You greedy chubby.

1047
00:33:36,010 --> 00:33:38,010
I've never been insulted
by a bird before.

1048
00:33:38,720 --> 00:33:40,020
Keep it up, and you'll be my food.

1049
00:33:40,020 --> 00:33:40,620
Come here.

1050
00:33:40,620 --> 00:33:41,120
Hm?

1051
00:33:42,040 --> 00:33:42,550
Come here.

1052
00:33:44,950 --> 00:33:45,450
Oops!

1053
00:33:47,090 --> 00:33:47,780
Wow...

1054
00:33:48,020 --> 00:33:48,980
You pooped?

1055
00:33:51,610 --> 00:33:52,150
What?

1056
00:33:53,210 --> 00:33:54,770
Why are your legs sticking up like that?

1057
00:33:55,890 --> 00:33:56,620
Duidui?

1058
00:33:57,640 --> 00:33:58,410
Duidui?

1059
00:33:58,410 --> 00:33:59,120
Sleepy?

1060
00:34:00,890 --> 00:34:02,580
Whoa!

1061
00:34:05,170 --> 00:34:07,750
I want to poke you with my stick.

1062
00:34:09,520 --> 00:34:10,730
Duidui's killer...

1063
00:34:12,179 --> 00:34:13,090
is Guard Dum.

1064
00:34:17,620 --> 00:34:18,820
Mr. Dodo...

1065
00:34:19,400 --> 00:34:20,199
Mr. Dodo,

1066
00:34:20,199 --> 00:34:21,920
please don't replace us.

1067
00:34:21,920 --> 00:34:24,020
This is all my fault.

1068
00:34:24,020 --> 00:34:24,920
And...

1069
00:34:24,920 --> 00:34:25,929
I promise...

1070
00:34:25,929 --> 00:34:28,420
that I won't waste your time
in the next scenes.

1071
00:34:31,050 --> 00:34:31,929
Please?

1072
00:34:32,179 --> 00:34:33,590
Yes, Mr. Dodo.

1073
00:34:33,929 --> 00:34:35,610
If you replace our extras,

1074
00:34:35,840 --> 00:34:38,000
we might not be able to
use the costumes we have.

1075
00:34:38,000 --> 00:34:39,330
And that might be

1076
00:34:40,179 --> 00:34:41,800
a bigger waste of your time.

1077
00:34:43,080 --> 00:34:44,400
If you can't do it, just leave.

1078
00:34:46,150 --> 00:34:46,929
The sponsor

1079
00:34:46,929 --> 00:34:48,550
invested this much

1080
00:34:49,370 --> 00:34:50,760
because of me.

1081
00:34:52,040 --> 00:34:54,000
Do you know who's important here?

1082
00:34:54,690 --> 00:34:57,300
Do you think this movie
could happen without me?

1083
00:34:58,760 --> 00:34:59,500
Will you,

1084
00:34:59,500 --> 00:35:00,080
you,

1085
00:35:00,290 --> 00:35:01,610
you, and you

1086
00:35:01,750 --> 00:35:02,950
have jobs?!

1087
00:35:08,600 --> 00:35:09,170
Hey.

1088
00:35:10,010 --> 00:35:11,560
Do you think you got this far

1089
00:35:12,000 --> 00:35:13,170
all on your own?

1090
00:35:15,570 --> 00:35:16,440
Yes!

1091
00:35:16,920 --> 00:35:18,660
It's all because of my looks.

1092
00:35:21,140 --> 00:35:23,000
You all have jobs

1093
00:35:23,790 --> 00:35:25,370
thanks to my good looks.

1094
00:35:27,570 --> 00:35:29,000
If we're talking about good looks,

1095
00:35:29,000 --> 00:35:30,260
I could also be the lead actor.

1096
00:35:31,490 --> 00:35:33,200
But I'm trying to prove to everyone

1097
00:35:33,660 --> 00:35:35,170
that I can play various roles.

1098
00:35:36,650 --> 00:35:37,910
And not rely solely on my looks,

1099
00:35:38,280 --> 00:35:39,440
which will fade as I age.

1100
00:35:40,900 --> 00:35:42,550
What a narcissistic speech.

1101
00:35:42,550 --> 00:35:43,210
But...

1102
00:35:43,210 --> 00:35:44,580
he said it in such a cool way.

1103
00:35:44,580 --> 00:35:45,330
Mm...

1104
00:35:48,280 --> 00:35:50,250
Do you think a movie
only needs one lead actor?

1105
00:35:52,040 --> 00:35:53,170
The cameramen,

1106
00:35:53,690 --> 00:35:54,550
lighting team,

1107
00:35:55,000 --> 00:35:55,750
and prop team

1108
00:35:56,480 --> 00:35:58,750
are the ones who make
beautiful cinematography possible.

1109
00:36:01,120 --> 00:36:02,100
There are extras

1110
00:36:03,260 --> 00:36:04,800
who liven up the movie.

1111
00:36:05,720 --> 00:36:06,760
You need makeup artists,

1112
00:36:07,580 --> 00:36:08,300
hair stylists,

1113
00:36:08,520 --> 00:36:09,320
the costume team,

1114
00:36:10,610 --> 00:36:11,770
and the cook.

1115
00:36:12,780 --> 00:36:14,950
If not for them, you wouldn't
be standing right here!

1116
00:36:16,640 --> 00:36:18,210
Everyone is equally important,

1117
00:36:19,730 --> 00:36:21,870
so treat everyone as equals.

1118
00:36:37,750 --> 00:36:38,460
Dax,

1119
00:36:38,820 --> 00:36:39,420
that's enough.

1120
00:36:39,420 --> 00:36:40,800
We're all going to be fired.

1121
00:36:41,130 --> 00:36:41,800
Stop...

1122
00:36:41,800 --> 00:36:42,780
I agree...

1123
00:36:42,780 --> 00:36:44,460
with what Dax said, though.

1124
00:36:44,780 --> 00:36:45,570
Right, everyone?

1125
00:36:45,570 --> 00:36:46,620
- Yes!
- Yes!

1126
00:36:46,620 --> 00:36:47,180
- Yes!
- Dax!

1127
00:36:47,180 --> 00:36:48,550
- Dax! Dax!
- Dax! Dax!

1128
00:36:48,700 --> 00:36:50,240
- Dax!
- Dax!

1129
00:36:50,360 --> 00:36:51,340
- Dax!
- Dax!

1130
00:36:51,340 --> 00:36:52,500
- Enough!
- Dax!

1131
00:36:53,050 --> 00:36:53,810
Director,

1132
00:36:53,840 --> 00:36:54,880
fire the entire crew.

1133
00:36:55,450 --> 00:36:56,300
Are you serious?

1134
00:37:01,620 --> 00:37:03,200
You left me no choice.

1135
00:37:05,880 --> 00:37:06,800
What are you going to do?

1136
00:37:06,800 --> 00:37:08,130
Do you think posting
this on social media...

1137
00:37:08,130 --> 00:37:09,730
will make them believe
an insignificant extra like you?!

1138
00:37:17,880 --> 00:37:18,550
Hello?

1139
00:37:18,550 --> 00:37:19,650
Uh... Yes.

1140
00:37:19,750 --> 00:37:20,580
Pardon me?

1141
00:37:21,660 --> 00:37:22,150
Uh...

1142
00:37:23,020 --> 00:37:23,580
Okay.

1143
00:37:24,140 --> 00:37:24,960
I'll arrange that right away.

1144
00:37:27,940 --> 00:37:28,800
Look,

1145
00:37:29,210 --> 00:37:30,650
the higher-ups are going to take action.

1146
00:37:32,010 --> 00:37:33,800
Prepare to lose your jobs.

1147
00:37:33,890 --> 00:37:34,980
The person who is losing their job

1148
00:37:35,460 --> 00:37:36,480
is you!

1149
00:37:37,750 --> 00:37:38,680
You doofus.

1150
00:37:38,680 --> 00:37:39,490
- Oh!
- Ooh!

1151
00:37:39,630 --> 00:37:42,080
The higher-ups told me
to replace the lead actor.

1152
00:37:42,100 --> 00:37:42,760
Huh?!

1153
00:37:45,730 --> 00:37:47,220
If you do that,
what will the sponsor think?

1154
00:37:47,220 --> 00:37:49,980
Our sponsor was the one
who told me to replace you.

1155
00:37:50,970 --> 00:37:54,320
They don't want an ambassador
who likes to put others down.

1156
00:37:54,320 --> 00:37:56,280
It tarnishes the brand's image!

1157
00:37:57,540 --> 00:37:59,090
And if you have any problems,

1158
00:37:59,330 --> 00:38:00,590
they said...

1159
00:38:00,980 --> 00:38:02,800
you can talk to the president's son.

1160
00:38:18,160 --> 00:38:18,980
Huh?

1161
00:38:18,980 --> 00:38:19,750
- Whoa.
- Yes!

1162
00:38:21,140 --> 00:38:22,910
I'm the president's son.

1163
00:38:23,600 --> 00:38:24,550
The president's son?

1164
00:38:25,940 --> 00:38:27,540
I didn't want to do this,

1165
00:38:28,000 --> 00:38:30,400
but everyone here is equally important.

1166
00:38:30,400 --> 00:38:32,440
Someone like you

1167
00:38:32,440 --> 00:38:33,940
needs to be taught a lesson.

1168
00:38:34,510 --> 00:38:36,840
You were acting all high
and mighty earlier,

1169
00:38:36,840 --> 00:38:38,950
but now you look like a kicked puppy.

1170
00:38:40,150 --> 00:38:41,800
Ooh, kicked puppy.

1171
00:38:41,800 --> 00:38:43,420
- Go, go, leave.
- Kicked puppy.

1172
00:38:45,240 --> 00:38:46,450
Um, Director?

1173
00:38:46,770 --> 00:38:47,350
Who...

1174
00:38:47,720 --> 00:38:48,550
will be the lead actor now?

1175
00:38:48,900 --> 00:38:49,750
Lead actor, huh?

1176
00:38:50,950 --> 00:38:51,500
I wonder who.

1177
00:38:51,660 --> 00:38:52,530
- Huh?
- Oh?

1178
00:38:52,890 --> 00:38:53,920
Or...

1179
00:38:53,920 --> 00:38:54,810
What about you, Dax?

1180
00:38:55,260 --> 00:38:56,320
I know I'm handsome.

1181
00:38:56,320 --> 00:38:56,690
Mm.

1182
00:38:56,690 --> 00:38:57,530
I know I'm cool.

1183
00:38:57,530 --> 00:38:58,150
Mm.

1184
00:38:58,150 --> 00:38:58,780
But I...

1185
00:38:59,130 --> 00:39:00,510
still aspire

1186
00:39:01,520 --> 00:39:03,320
to be the best extra there is!

1187
00:39:03,840 --> 00:39:04,780
- Ugh...
- Huh?

1188
00:39:04,780 --> 00:39:05,770
He's a weird one,

1189
00:39:05,770 --> 00:39:06,920
turning down a lead role like that.

1190
00:39:06,920 --> 00:39:08,290
Yeah. What was he
acting all cool for earlier?

1191
00:39:08,290 --> 00:39:08,820
Yeah.

1192
00:39:09,370 --> 00:39:10,150
What about me, Mom?

1193
00:39:10,290 --> 00:39:11,100
- Hm?
- Oh.

1194
00:39:12,330 --> 00:39:13,540
- Hey, he's back.
- What should we do?

1195
00:39:15,210 --> 00:39:16,150
Mr. Dim.

1196
00:39:20,370 --> 00:39:21,420
Mr. Dim...

1197
00:39:21,600 --> 00:39:22,570
Mr. Dim...

1198
00:39:22,850 --> 00:39:24,800
I'm so sorry, Mr. Dim.

1199
00:39:25,080 --> 00:39:27,500
Mr. Dim, if you fire me,

1200
00:39:27,520 --> 00:39:28,810
it will be a hassle for everyone.

1201
00:39:28,830 --> 00:39:30,610
It's also a waste of time.

1202
00:39:31,050 --> 00:39:32,950
Mr. Dim, please forgive me.

1203
00:39:33,220 --> 00:39:34,420
Mr. Dim, I promise

1204
00:39:34,420 --> 00:39:36,770
I won't act like this in front of you again.

1205
00:39:37,000 --> 00:39:39,130
Please let me continue being the lead actor,

1206
00:39:39,620 --> 00:39:40,780
Mr. Dim...

1207
00:39:41,610 --> 00:39:43,840
- Please...
- Promise you'll behave?

1208
00:39:44,020 --> 00:39:44,800
Yes,

1209
00:39:44,800 --> 00:39:45,560
I promise.

1210
00:39:49,240 --> 00:39:50,450
You'll let me...

1211
00:39:50,450 --> 00:39:51,810
remain the lead actor, right?

1212
00:39:52,010 --> 00:39:52,760
Mr. Dim?

1213
00:39:53,350 --> 00:39:54,250
Mr. Dim?

1214
00:39:55,340 --> 00:39:56,460
Mr. Dim...

1215
00:39:56,820 --> 00:39:57,440
Hm?

1216
00:39:57,440 --> 00:39:58,500
You'll let me remain the lead actor, right?

1217
00:39:58,780 --> 00:39:59,760
What should I do?

1218
00:40:00,660 --> 00:40:01,570
Mr. Dim.

1219
00:40:01,570 --> 00:40:02,780
Mr. Dim, wait.

1220
00:40:02,780 --> 00:40:04,040
- Please let me be the lead actor.
- I'll think about it.

1221
00:40:04,040 --> 00:40:05,020
Mr. Dim.

1222
00:40:05,620 --> 00:40:06,550
Mr. Dim, wait.

1223
00:40:06,820 --> 00:40:08,780
- Whoa...
- Oh...

1224
00:40:08,950 --> 00:40:10,150
He completely changed, huh?

1225
00:40:10,320 --> 00:40:11,160
Mm.

1226
00:40:11,160 --> 00:40:12,900
Is he a chameleon or something?

1227
00:40:12,900 --> 00:40:13,790
Right?

1228
00:40:14,010 --> 00:40:15,120
I didn't do it!

1229
00:40:15,530 --> 00:40:17,740
Duidui died before I even touched it.

1230
00:40:17,930 --> 00:40:20,130
It might have died from shock

1231
00:40:20,420 --> 00:40:21,970
after seeing an
Asian black bear standing nearby.

1232
00:40:22,290 --> 00:40:23,390
- Whoa...
- Hey!

1233
00:40:24,330 --> 00:40:25,580
Stop badmouthing my brother!

1234
00:40:25,760 --> 00:40:27,630
He isn't an Asian black bear.

1235
00:40:27,900 --> 00:40:29,350
The most I'll allow is a bearcat.

1236
00:40:29,490 --> 00:40:30,440
Or maybe a sun bear.

1237
00:40:31,220 --> 00:40:32,160
Ooh, cute.

1238
00:40:32,160 --> 00:40:33,170
Ca-caw.

1239
00:40:33,170 --> 00:40:33,960
Stop it.

1240
00:40:35,460 --> 00:40:36,550
I can see that

1241
00:40:37,220 --> 00:40:39,170
Guard Dum really didn't
do anything to the bird.

1242
00:40:40,650 --> 00:40:42,170
To keep things fair,

1243
00:40:42,890 --> 00:40:44,950
why don't we take it to the vet

1244
00:40:45,220 --> 00:40:46,150
to find out the cause of death?

1245
00:40:46,150 --> 00:40:47,700
- Yeah, yeah.
- Great idea.

1246
00:40:47,700 --> 00:40:50,570
Are you trying to
avoid paying me 50,000 baht?

1247
00:40:51,690 --> 00:40:52,970
What happened to Duidui?

1248
00:40:54,970 --> 00:40:57,880
[Day, occupation: veterinarian]

1249
00:40:58,560 --> 00:41:00,050
Here he is, the vet.

1250
00:41:00,310 --> 00:41:01,390
Day, it's him.

1251
00:41:01,690 --> 00:41:03,200
He killed our Duidui.

1252
00:41:03,200 --> 00:41:03,700
What?

1253
00:41:03,700 --> 00:41:05,170
He's refusing to take responsibility.

1254
00:41:05,650 --> 00:41:06,550
Duidui is dead?

1255
00:41:06,550 --> 00:41:07,280
Mm.

1256
00:41:07,580 --> 00:41:08,450
Duidui!

1257
00:41:08,720 --> 00:41:09,480
Duidui!

1258
00:41:09,840 --> 00:41:11,040
Peep, peep, peep.

1259
00:41:11,210 --> 00:41:13,100
Ook, ook, ook.

1260
00:41:13,260 --> 00:41:14,620
Peep, peep, peep.

1261
00:41:14,620 --> 00:41:16,680
Ook, ook, ook.

1262
00:41:17,810 --> 00:41:18,550
Hey...

1263
00:41:20,380 --> 00:41:22,400
Did anyone feed Duidui anything?

1264
00:41:23,160 --> 00:41:23,900
Uh...

1265
00:41:23,900 --> 00:41:24,920
Duidui had...

1266
00:41:24,920 --> 00:41:26,950
ooh-ah-ah.

1267
00:41:27,090 --> 00:41:29,090
Ook, ook, ook.

1268
00:41:29,090 --> 00:41:30,250
- Hey!
- Ugh!

1269
00:41:30,550 --> 00:41:31,040
What the heck?

1270
00:41:31,040 --> 00:41:32,460
Allow me to answer.

1271
00:41:33,820 --> 00:41:36,250
Ever since we caught it,
all we've given it

1272
00:41:36,550 --> 00:41:37,930
is the water in the tray.

1273
00:41:38,140 --> 00:41:40,450
You gave it dirty tap water, didn't you?

1274
00:41:41,810 --> 00:41:43,180
Pay me 50,000 baht.

1275
00:41:43,180 --> 00:41:44,000
Whoa...

1276
00:41:49,330 --> 00:41:50,530
Shut up, Duong.

1277
00:41:52,480 --> 00:41:54,420
You're acting like you care about Duidui

1278
00:41:54,420 --> 00:41:56,280
only because you want
money from them, aren't you?

1279
00:41:56,730 --> 00:41:58,480
You didn't seem to care
when Duidui was still alive.

1280
00:41:59,800 --> 00:42:00,550
What?

1281
00:42:00,550 --> 00:42:02,260
You're pretending that you care

1282
00:42:02,560 --> 00:42:04,150
just to get money from us?

1283
00:42:05,730 --> 00:42:07,750
If he actually takes good care of Duidui,

1284
00:42:07,980 --> 00:42:09,650
he won't let it starve.

1285
00:42:09,650 --> 00:42:11,060
He left it no choice
but to fly out to find food,

1286
00:42:11,060 --> 00:42:12,930
and it ended up
dying from diarrhea like this.

1287
00:42:12,930 --> 00:42:14,300
It died from diarrhea...

1288
00:42:14,480 --> 00:42:15,030
So,

1289
00:42:15,490 --> 00:42:16,660
the bird wasn't killed,

1290
00:42:16,900 --> 00:42:18,420
but it died from diarrhea?

1291
00:42:18,420 --> 00:42:19,020
Mm.

1292
00:42:19,360 --> 00:42:20,730
No wonder it pooped so much.

1293
00:42:20,730 --> 00:42:21,440
Hey, Day.

1294
00:42:22,010 --> 00:42:23,040
Can you stop being stupid?

1295
00:42:23,180 --> 00:42:24,800
Since the bird died,

1296
00:42:25,540 --> 00:42:27,210
we could've gotten some money from them.

1297
00:42:28,700 --> 00:42:29,650
Does this mean...

1298
00:42:30,420 --> 00:42:32,020
you're trying to steal from us?

1299
00:42:33,840 --> 00:42:35,350
Don't accuse me like that, Officer.

1300
00:42:35,350 --> 00:42:37,540
I'm just trying to protect his interests.

1301
00:42:38,880 --> 00:42:39,950
Is it really for me?

1302
00:42:40,150 --> 00:42:41,280
Or is it for yourself?

1303
00:42:41,660 --> 00:42:43,520
I went to find a new place to rent,

1304
00:42:43,520 --> 00:42:45,400
so I had to leave Duidui with you.

1305
00:42:45,850 --> 00:42:47,940
You even charged me for looking after it.

1306
00:42:48,170 --> 00:42:50,260
You were the one who caused its death,

1307
00:42:50,950 --> 00:42:52,320
so shouldn't you take responsibility?

1308
00:42:56,040 --> 00:42:57,480
Why am I the one responsible?

1309
00:42:58,150 --> 00:42:59,500
The bird is already dead,

1310
00:42:59,660 --> 00:43:01,050
and you've already moved away.

1311
00:43:01,330 --> 00:43:02,520
Isn't that the end of it?

1312
00:43:09,090 --> 00:43:09,760
Huh?

1313
00:43:10,200 --> 00:43:11,900
Your parents are buying stock
in Tim's pot business?

1314
00:43:13,900 --> 00:43:15,130
Tell your parents this.

1315
00:43:15,130 --> 00:43:15,460
What?

1316
00:43:15,460 --> 00:43:16,560
They should stop trading stocks.

1317
00:43:18,550 --> 00:43:19,570
Look at what they pick...

1318
00:43:22,220 --> 00:43:23,250
Duidui...

1319
00:43:23,690 --> 00:43:24,890
I'm sorry for your loss, Mr. Day.

1320
00:43:25,210 --> 00:43:26,600
This is my fault.

1321
00:43:27,180 --> 00:43:29,010
I shouldn't have left Duidui with Duong.

1322
00:43:30,360 --> 00:43:31,520
I'm sorry, dear.

1323
00:43:32,380 --> 00:43:33,260
Duidui...

1324
00:43:33,900 --> 00:43:34,650
Oh, dear...

1325
00:43:34,650 --> 00:43:37,500
Peep, peep, peep.

1326
00:43:37,750 --> 00:43:38,740
Ook, ook, ook.

1327
00:43:38,950 --> 00:43:40,520
Ooh-ah-ah.

1328
00:43:40,520 --> 00:43:42,250
Ha-ha-ha.

1329
00:43:42,250 --> 00:43:43,100
Oh, no...

1330
00:43:43,100 --> 00:43:44,780
My poor Duidui...

1331
00:43:44,780 --> 00:43:45,860
Poor thing...

1332
00:43:46,480 --> 00:43:48,140
Is there a monkey in that cage?

1333
00:43:51,760 --> 00:43:53,130
I feel bad for him,

1334
00:43:53,690 --> 00:43:55,050
losing his bird like that.

1335
00:43:56,000 --> 00:43:57,580
He's probably very sad.

1336
00:43:59,570 --> 00:44:00,490
Yeah.

1337
00:44:00,720 --> 00:44:02,800
If I were him, I'd be heartbroken, too.

1338
00:44:08,010 --> 00:44:08,820
Ugh!

1339
00:44:08,820 --> 00:44:10,040
What's with you sneakily holding my hand?

1340
00:44:11,930 --> 00:44:13,220
Duidui, you poor thing.

1341
00:44:14,950 --> 00:44:15,810
You passed away...

1342
00:44:16,600 --> 00:44:17,960
without ever saying...

1343
00:44:18,700 --> 00:44:19,750
Dollar has a great body.

1344
00:44:20,040 --> 00:44:20,570
Ugh...

1345
00:44:20,770 --> 00:44:22,150
It probably had so much left unsaid.

1346
00:44:23,350 --> 00:44:24,550
Everyone in this dorm...

1347
00:44:24,740 --> 00:44:25,750
Dollar has a great body.

1348
00:44:27,400 --> 00:44:28,440
- Big muscles.
- You got those big muscles

1349
00:44:28,440 --> 00:44:29,760
by injecting baking soda into them, right?

1350
00:44:30,730 --> 00:44:31,490
I didn't.

1351
00:44:36,850 --> 00:44:39,020
[The D Dorm]

1352
00:44:42,550 --> 00:44:43,750
Dobby,

1353
00:44:44,840 --> 00:44:46,150
his bird is already dead.

1354
00:44:46,320 --> 00:44:49,750
Why are you so sad about it?

1355
00:44:49,920 --> 00:44:52,800
I saw you sitting there
looking glum for a while.

1356
00:44:54,690 --> 00:44:55,450
What?

1357
00:44:56,950 --> 00:45:00,000
Or is it that you want
to learn how to speak like a bird?

1358
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:02,060
I can teach you that.

1359
00:45:03,610 --> 00:45:04,800
Say...

1360
00:45:05,020 --> 00:45:07,750
Chu-cao, chu-cao, chu-cao.

1361
00:45:07,750 --> 00:45:09,100
Chu-cao, chu-cao.

1362
00:45:09,130 --> 00:45:10,530
Chu-cao, chu-cao, chu-cao.

1363
00:45:16,150 --> 00:45:16,760
Grandpa,

1364
00:45:18,550 --> 00:45:20,000
Duong thinks that...

1365
00:45:20,380 --> 00:45:22,150
now that the bird is dead,
everything is over.

1366
00:45:22,530 --> 00:45:24,370
He doesn't have to take
responsibility for it.

1367
00:45:24,760 --> 00:45:26,220
Do you think he's selfish?

1368
00:45:26,610 --> 00:45:28,150
He sure is selfish.

1369
00:45:30,320 --> 00:45:31,750
Don't you think
you're being selfish as well?

1370
00:45:31,940 --> 00:45:32,760
Nonsense.

1371
00:45:33,530 --> 00:45:34,780
How am I selfish?

1372
00:45:35,050 --> 00:45:37,750
I heard everything
you said to Uncle Tong on the rooftop.

1373
00:45:38,260 --> 00:45:40,300
I just want to take this secret

1374
00:45:40,300 --> 00:45:43,140
to my grave.

1375
00:45:44,200 --> 00:45:45,410
Tell me honestly, Grandpa.

1376
00:45:47,160 --> 00:45:48,550
Did you ever love my mother?

1377
00:45:49,180 --> 00:45:49,750
I did.

1378
00:45:49,880 --> 00:45:50,950
If you did,

1379
00:45:52,450 --> 00:45:55,340
why are you letting her
carry all this guilt on her shoulders?

1380
00:45:55,900 --> 00:45:58,450
You think everything is over
after you passed away, huh?

1381
00:45:59,090 --> 00:45:59,770
Did you know?

1382
00:46:00,340 --> 00:46:01,750
On the day you passed away,

1383
00:46:02,240 --> 00:46:03,800
Mom was crying.

1384
00:46:03,800 --> 00:46:05,960
She blamed herself, thinking
it was her fault for leaving you behind.

1385
00:46:05,960 --> 00:46:08,080
When in fact, you were the one

1386
00:46:08,410 --> 00:46:10,370
who drove my mother away.

1387
00:46:15,500 --> 00:46:16,610
I did not know...

1388
00:46:18,570 --> 00:46:20,590
I thought she was happy.

1389
00:46:22,150 --> 00:46:23,350
I thought...

1390
00:46:25,290 --> 00:46:26,970
she had already forgotten about me...

1391
00:46:28,680 --> 00:46:30,200
I never knew...

1392
00:46:30,700 --> 00:46:32,170
Then carry that turtle shell

1393
00:46:33,120 --> 00:46:34,770
until you understand how my mother felt

1394
00:46:35,900 --> 00:46:37,260
carrying all that guilt.

1395
00:46:41,010 --> 00:46:42,100
Dobby...

1396
00:47:01,260 --> 00:47:02,070
I choose this card.

